{
  "_comment": [
    "Canonical MCP wiring for Claude Code ↔ MPM.",
    "",
    "Source of truth: this file is the canonical template. The install",
    "script (install.sh) materializes it into ~/.claude/.mcp.json with",
    "absolute paths substituted. ${HOME} is intentionally used here so the",
    "template is portable across machines; the install script replaces it.",
    "",
    "Why mpm-mcp, not the opencode-mpm or pi-mpm TypeScript adapters:",
    "Claude Code's native extension surface is MCP. The mpm-mcp binary IS",
    "the agent-facing machine interface. The default initial MCP surface",
    "is 3 tools (mpm_memory, mpm_context, mpm_help); the full 22-tool",
    "substrate registry is restored when MPM_EXPOSE_ALL_TOOLS=1 is set on",
    "the MCP env block below.",
    "Re-using the same MCP server that OpenClaw wires means every agent on",
    "the host converges on the same canonical substrate with no per-agent",
    "reimplementation.",
    "",
    "Why MPM_WORKSPACE=${HOME}/.mpm: the canonical install root has its",
    "src/db/mpm.db hardlinked to the actual workspace DB, so the install",
    "root is a portable, deterministic workspace handle that works on any",
    "machine that has performed 'make install' (no dependence on the user's",
    "particular MPM_WORKSPACE env var layout). The health_check response",
    "carries the resolved db_path so operators can verify convergence.",
    "",
    "Why MPM_FRAMEWORK=claude-code:",
    "this is the canonical framework-identification env var for mpm-mcp",
    "(see internal/core/mpmcli/mpmcli.go: ActiveContextFromEnv reads MPM_FRAMEWORK",
    "and populates ActiveContext.FrameworkName; see README \u00a71827 for the transport",
    "contract). mpm-mcp's audit_hook (cmd/mpm-mcp/audit_hook.go) and",
    "artifact_provenance writes both use ac.FrameworkName as the canonical source.",
    "Without this var, framework_name falls through to the default 'mcp' value and",
    "claude-code-originated artifact writes are misattributed. Standard ids are",
    "documented at README \u00a71820: 'openclaw', 'opencode', 'pi', 'claude-code', 'hermes'.",
    "",
    "Actor-kind classification: mpm-mcp's tool_invocations path hardcodes",
    "actor_kind='agent' for every MCP server tool call (cmd/mpm-mcp/audit_hook.go:46).",
    "The artifact_provenance.actor_kind column is populated by the provenance",
    "resolver (internal/core/provenance.go NewFromEnv + Resolve), which consumes",
    "MPM_PROVENANCE_* env vars and falls back to the empty string when unset.",
    "There is no MPM_FRAMEWORK-equivalent env var for actor_kind in the legacy wire",
    "contract; we accept the default 'agent' attribution for claude-code MCP calls",
    "rather than fabricate a different label. Don't add MPM_PROVENANCE_ACTOR_KIND",
    "to this template \u2014 it's an empty override with no documentary backing, and we",
    "do not want to lie about provenance semantics.",
    "",
    "Explicitly NOT set in this template, by design:",
    "  - MPM_PROVENANCE_MODEL: the actual model in use is dynamic per session",
    "    (MiniMax-M2.7, MiniMax-M3, etc.) and changes between turns. A static value",
    "    in this config would be a fabrication. Leave NULL/empty.",
    "  - MPM_PROVENANCE_INVOCATION_ID / PARENT_INVOCATION_ID / MPM_FRAMEWORK_INVOCATION_ID:",
    "    these must be generated dynamically per invocation by the framework layer.",
    "    They have no sensible static value. Do not add them here.",
    "  - MPM_PROVENANCE_ACTOR_KIND=agent: redundant with mpm-mcp's audit_hook default.",
    "    Adding it would imply a contract that this codebase does not implement.",
    "",
    "Provenance contract: observational, not authoritative. Artifact correctness",
    "must remain independent of provenance availability; missing or incorrect",
    "provenance must never block or poison an artifact transaction."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "mpm": {
      "command": "${HOME}/.mpm/bin/mpm-mcp",
      "args": [],
      "env": {
        "MPM_WORKSPACE": "${HOME}/.mpm",
        "MPM_FRAMEWORK": "claude-code"
      }
    }
  }
}
